    file(path        = core/xmq.ixml
         size        = 6762
         sha256      = e4170038ed010eb9f7e2e1e3121fbed65d8991d76ffc2ff96a209b8c00f0b41a
         mtime       = 2026-11-20T20:49:16Z
         version     = 2a
         description = 'The xmq language in ixml.
                        by Fredrik Öhrström (c) 2024-2026 spdx: MIT

                        Rewritten with the not operator ! and greedy tokens, so that the grammar
                        has a single parse and works with the LL(*) parser generator. A greedy
                        token ends with !c where c is a rule that matches one character, eg
                        name = ..., -namechar*, !namechar.

                        The parse tree is turned into the xml dom of the xmq document by xmq.xslq:

                            xmq xmq.ixml input.xmq transform xmq.xslq

                        gives the same document as xmq input.xmq. The tree:

                            xmq { node* }
                            node = element(name) { attributes? children? }
                                 | keyvalue(name) { attributes? value }
                                 | quote | entity | comment { part+ } | line_comment
                                 | doctype { value } | pi(name) { value } | xml
                            attributes { attr(name) { value? }* }
                            children { node* }
                            value = text | quote | entity | compound { (quote | entity)* }

                        Quotes, comments and texts keep their raw content (without the quote
                        chars and comment markers), the incidental indentation is removed by
                        xmq.xslq like the xmq parser does. An entity keeps its name without & and ;
                        eg nbsp or #10.')
    file(path        = core/xmq.xslq
         size        = 30253
         sha256      = ab1b945432145775d5eda9fbb1250c9b425a94029b5482e5eeb160a58028b579
         mtime       = 2026-11-20T20:49:16Z
         version     = 2a
         description = 'Build the xmq document from the parse tree of xmq.ixml.
                        by Fredrik Öhrström (c) 2024-2026 spdx: MIT

                            xmq xmq.ixml input.xmq transform xmq.xslq

                        gives the same document as xmq input.xmq. The element and attribute
                        names come from the name attributes, the namespaces from the xmlns
                        declarations, quotes and comments get their incidental indentation
                        removed with the same rules as xmq_trim_quote in xmq.c.

                        What xslt 1.0 cannot create (entity references, the doctype, embedded
                        xml, empty texts, unused namespace declarations, undeclared prefixes) is
                        output as marker elements in the namespace https://libxmq.org/xmq/markers
                        that xmq replaces after the transform, see xmq_replace_transform_markers.')
