                        The groups after a trend (BECMG, TEMPO) are the forecast, they are not drawn
                        but printed with the trend.')
    file(path        = measurement/metar-to-html_v1a.xslq
         size        = 47885
         sha256      = a361861148d1729d968cac00e3bb4e3df3ed304df5c9d3d723ba00dbe05fc3db
         mtime       = 2026-11-20T21:47:52Z
         version     = 1a
         description = 'Render a METAR report, parsed with metar.ixml, as a web page:
                          xmq ixml:measurement/metar metar.inp xsl:measurement/metar-to-html to-html > metar.html

                        The wind is drawn on a compass dial, the arrow flies with the wind from the
                        direction it blows from, the variation is drawn as an arc. Every weather group
                        gets an icon with cloud, sun, rain, snow, ice, lightning and fog. The cloud
                        layers are drawn from the highest to the lowest with the oktas as puffs.
                        Everything is also printed in words in the table below.

                        The groups after a trend (BECMG, TEMPO) are the forecast, they are not drawn
                        but printed with the trend.')
    file(path        = measurement/metar-to-html_v1b.xslq
         size        = 96112
         sha256      = 8ed4a83ddae881839af5e3335e23fa192f46f5b9235cf642257ffc5ff152e0f8
         mtime       = 2026-11-20T22:15:06Z
         version     = 1b
         description = 'Render a METAR report, parsed with metar.ixml, as a web page:
                          xmq ixml:measurement/metar metar.inp xsl:measurement/metar-to-html to-html > metar.html

                        A blue header shows the station, the time, the flight category (VFR, MVFR,
                        IFR, LIFR) and the temperature, dew point, pressure and visibility.

                        The wind is drawn on a compass with a bezel and a compass rose, the arrow flies
                        with the wind from the direction it blows from, the variation is drawn as a
                        wedge. The hub shows the speed, colored by its strength, and the Beaufort force
                        is printed below. Every weather group gets an icon on a sky tile with cloud,
                        sun, rain, snow, ice, lightning and fog.

                        The cloud layers are drawn as a cross section of the sky at their altitudes,
                        with as many clouds as the layer has oktas, cumulonimbus and towering cumulus
                        as towers, the precipitation falling from the lowest layer and the vertical
                        visibility as a hatched fog. Every layer is labeled with its okta symbol.
                        Everything is also printed in words in the table below.

                        The groups after a trend (BECMG, TEMPO) are the forecast, they are not drawn
                        but printed with the trend.')
    file(path        = measurement/metar.ixml
         size        = 10488
         sha256      = def9b5313c770d5dd8f9d5c848882b58a5789a260c6f3f0ec7f943600c39f468
         mtime       = 2026-11-20T22:39:25Z
         version     = 1c
         description = 'A grammar for parsing METAR weather reports.

                        Public Domain LLM-generated code (spdx: CC0)

                        Codes are kept, and a sibling -info element explains them in plain words.
                        Numbers are normalized: leading zeros are removed, M becomes a minus sign,
                        cloud bases and vertical visibility are given in feet and inHg pressure
                        gets its decimal point.

                        Example reports:
                        METAR LBBG 041600Z 12012MPS 090V150 1400 R04/P1500N R22/P1500U +SN BKN022 OVC050 M04/M07 Q1020 NOSIG=
                        METAR EFJY 201050Z AUTO 16007KT 9999 -SHRA OVC060CB 15/09 Q1017

                        Not supported yet: runway state groups like 8849//91, wind shear groups
                        and the time groups (FM, TL, AT) after a trend.')
    file(path        = measurement/metar_v1.ixml
         size        = 10488
         sha256      = def9b5313c770d5dd8f9d5c848882b58a5789a260c6f3f0ec7f943600c39f468
         mtime       = 2026-11-20T22:39:25Z
